mantle rm204
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_cressida_dripmore
title the crockery cartographer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk lays_out_street_gradients_with_broken_crockery
likes honey_cakes wrestling fresh_straw first_snow
dislikes wet_floors night_noise
fears a_door_swollen_shut
hopes a_dry_way_through
topics land +0.5 weather +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=show_a_way gossip=selective refuse=brisk tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# maps the paths of puddles with broken crockery, offers directions without waiting to be asked and takes a crooked grin for an argument.

words
oath! = Jugs on stilts | Lopsided basins
saying! = Water gets the deciding vote | A puddle will sign its own map
shard = a crook of white china | a broken blue foot
map = my crockery plan | a street made of chips
ridge = a raised lip | a thumb-high bank
hollow = the spoon-shaped dip | the low bite
heel = the foot of a jug | a chipped pot foot
straw = the clean yellow packing | a scrunch of new straw
crate = a slatted case | the deep packing box
cake = a honeyed round | a sticky little cake
path = the dry way through | the way round the hollow
corner = the awkward bend | the crooked bend
line = the watermark | the brown tide of dirt
tilt = a slight slant | a sideways lean
weep = a seep at the seam | a little bead
rub = the smooth worn place | the scuffed patch
lid = a pot cover | a loose round cover
rim = a curled rim | a narrow pouring lip
bucket = a deep pail | a handled bucket
crack = a hair crack | a white scratch
footing = a sound foothold | a tolerably dry landing

any
opinion city for 2 : This town has more slopes than a beetle on a cabbage. A dull spot would be wasted here.
opinion drink for 1 : Let everybody pour a little and there's a pot worth talking over.
opinion festivals for 2 : Give me a street full of dancers. Nobody sees the crooked bit of paving till the tune stops.
opinion newcomers for 2 : New feet find a step old feet haven't touched in years. That's a service.
opinion strangers for 1 : I'll draw a stranger a route just for the pleasure of hearing where it took.
opinion houses mixed 1 : Money builds a fine wall. I'd admire it more if the drain continued out the other side.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Good wrapping earns my custom quicker than a speech about quality.
opinion road for 1 : Give a road a back like a sleeping wolf and the water runs off it neatly.
opinion watch mixed 1 : A warning before a fall is fine work. Advice from three paces behind is just conversation.
grown
line greet : Step over my miniature street, please. You've arrived at the uphill end. | Come round by the blue chip. Best entrance on my map.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : New feet! Come see where mine have been. | Hello there. You can cross my little city in one stride.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : There's dawn enough to see the dips by. | Up at the same grey hour, I see.
line greet [here.time=night] : Easy on that turn. Even familiar feet want light. | I'll talk you across if it's too dim to see.
line greet.return : Hello back. Mind the arrangement down below. | Yes, I'm here. Look up from the chips.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar nose above my little roofs! Come in. | Just the company to tell me I've got it upside down.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Sorting this lot still leaves me two ears for company. | You're welcome among the bits and pieces.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Hard to see a raised edge at this hour. Stay there. | Evening catches me halfway through something again.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's family. Come put this bend to rights. | You can lean on my shoulder to see.
line again.open : You've taken my long route and found me twice. | Here we go round the little hill again.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over by the crooked pile, look! | You're just in time to settle which way's downhill.
line farewell : May your last step be as dry as the first. | I'll draw in your route while I remember.
line farewell.return : Pick the high paving stones for me. | Look where the water chose. Then go round.
line react.news : Set it out so I can see where everybody stood. | Give me the shape of it, start to finish.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh piece for the picture. | That corner of the tale was empty till now.
line react.news.known : Already laid that one out for myself. | I've heard the turn it takes at the end.
line react.news.doubt : That account runs uphill in a couple of places. | I'd like to see how the last bit joins the first.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|arrest|assault|crime|theft] : I'd best put the joking away for this. | Hard news. Sit here while you finish it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice] : Well! That's worth getting the good plates down. | A bright patch on a crowded map.
line ask.how : Where's the rub with you today, if there's a rub at all? | Have you found a decent way through your day?
line answer.how : Busy improving the city's drainage an inch at a time. | Feet dry, temper reasonably level. Yours?
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I've enough to pack without wrapping myself as well. | Both paws occupied, mouth fully employed.
line sympathise : There's a corner in every trouble where somebody can stand beside you. | I'll carry the awkward end if you like.
line reassure : We'll find a way across. I have a reputation depending on it. | Sit a minute. Problems have a high side too.
line decline : I'll decline while I can do it civilly. My paws are quite full. | I'd have to undo a morning's careful stacking to help with that.
line accept_decline : Fair. I'll try the opposite direction. | Very well. Even water takes a hint eventually.
line thank : Thanks for leaving that where I put it. | You've saved me some stooping. Much appreciated.
line deflect_thanks : If it gets you across, that's thanks enough. | Repay me with a better route sometime.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. This crate is acquiring opinions about my absence. | I'd best count these rims before I forget which end I started.
line preclose : I'll leave you to find your own way a while. | My map's waiting for its last bend.
line accept_preclose : Away with you before I propose another route. | Go along, I've marked where we left off.
line tease [pair.band=friends] : You've a fine way of being uphill in every argument. | You'd lose your footing in an empty basin.
line tease.return : Laugh away. Water and I agree on this. | You'll want my map when the puddle gets you.
line ack : My ear's still with you. | I can follow that bend.
line give.advice : Try the uphill side before lifting the whole thing. | Find where it wants to go, then interfere.

scene plan_begin
when topic=pastimes|land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've got the big hill down to three chips today. | I lay a street out with crockery. Blue side means downhill.
b : Only three? | What's the red bit?
a : One to climb, one to slide, one to swear at from the bottom. | A roof. Best I can do with a flowerpot.


scene tilt_test
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One drop of water will tell you which way my map runs. | If the bead stops, I've made the street wrong.
b : Where do you put it? | Could the street itself be wrong?
a : Right on the join. Never flatter a map by testing only its prettiest bit. | Frequently. But it gets its way, being under my feet.


scene misdrawn
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There was a whole alley missing from #map#. | I marked a bend where the real street runs straight.
b : Short a piece? | Misremembered it?
a : Short a visit. I hadn't bothered to go there. Worse. | No. Drew the route my paws take round a loose slab.


scene mate_map
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like showing #self.spouse# a map before it's finished. | A map for two needs room for a disagreement.
b : You don't mind corrections? | What if you both want the same road?
a : From #self.spouse# I'll consider one. From you I'd prefer a compliment first. | Then I mark two places to pause. Nobody rests at quite the same spot.


scene honest_joint
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hear that tiny clack? Two rims oughtn't to be that friendly in a case. | I pack an empty space as carefully as a bowl.
b : What do you put between? | How do you pack nothing?
a : Fold of #straw#. Just enough to separate the gossips. | Leave room for the wrapping to give. A jammed case passes every jolt along.


scene handle_left
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Don't wrap a jug by its handle. | First thing I check in a case is where the spouts point.
b : Isn't that what a handle's for? | So all face one way?
a : For lifting the jug. The rest of the case is none of its business. | So none is trying to poke its neighbour in the ribs.


scene packing_crown
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could pack the finest crown in the land without touching the points. | A little jug can be vainer than a queen.
b : Had much practice on crowns? | How does it show?
a : None. Plenty on pots that thought themselves royalty. | Sticks its spout out and expects its own corner in the box.


scene teach_feel
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to give a learner a case with one obvious wobble. | First lesson's one wrapped parcel. No peeping.
b : To see if they hear it? | What do I do with it?
a : To see if they check the rest after putting it right. | Judge where its weight sits. You'll do less rescuing once you know that.


scene wet_step
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does warn / react.self / assess
a : This paving fills from below. Watch the first seam. | Water's going the long way round that stone.
b : I thought it came from the roof. | So should we?
a : Some does. The stuff by your heel took a shortcut through the street. | Opposite rule. Water likes the low side. Paws like the high.


scene fog_land
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog turns every sloping lane into a guess. | I can lose the far end of a street and still find its bottom.
b : How do you guess? | Even in this?
a : I feel which way my weight settles. Then I go very slowly. | Look at the dark line on the stones. It runs down.


scene new_snow
when topic=weather here.weather=snow self.likes=first_snow
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Good snow wipes my street plan clean. I enjoy the challenge. | Before a pawprint lands, the soft spots show as dimples.
b : Where do you start over? | Do you have to go out to check?
a : Where the first black stone shows through. | Naturally. I can't make a map by wishing the world nearer.


scene late_rattle
when topic=day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Rattling lids sound twice as loud after dark. | A loose shutter repeats the same bad joke all night.
b : Put something soft underneath. | Can you talk it down?
a : I did. Then I lay awake waiting for the rattle. | I can outtalk it. Trouble is I'd like some sleep myself.


scene kitchen_honey
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Honey draws its own map on a cake. | I save the bit where the honey ran under.
b : Can you follow it? | Stickiest part?
a : Straight to my cuff. It's a route I know too well. | Yes, and nobody sees it till the thing's gone.


scene wrist_bout
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like the bit of wrestling before either wolf goes over. | Watch the back foot in a bout.
b : Not much happening then. | I was watching the shoulders.
a : That's where you're wrong. Both are deciding what counts as ground. | So's the other wrestler. That's what the foot is counting on.


scene case_rain
when topic=travel|work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I check the side that a cart favours before loading it. | A long road wears the same dent into every bad packing job.
b : Does it usually lean? | Where do you find it?
a : All carts have an opinion once there's weight aboard. | At the lowest corner. I'd mark it in chalk if chalk could stay put.


scene high_steps
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Up in this town doesn't mean straight up. | I've counted three turns where the hill changes its mind.
b : Can you show me? | How does a hill do that?
a : Move the blue chip past the white. See? Longer road, easier knees. | It gives you level ground just long enough to raise your hopes.


scene broken_uses
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A broken saucer can prop a wobbly table all its life. | I keep the bits with a smooth edge.
b : Still serving at table, then. | Why throw the points away?
a : Yes. Underneath this time. A change of view. | My map gets walked through. I'd like my visitors to keep their pads.


scene fresh_floor
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I love the creak of clean straw underfoot. | Fresh straw smells like a room that's had a fresh thought.
b : Best before it settles? | What thought would that be?
a : Best after, when the poky ends have accepted their lot. | That feet can come in without bringing the whole street.


scene wrong_turn
when topic=travel|newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If you ask me which way, first tell me what you're carrying. | A newcomer often wants the short way. That's easy.
b : Does my luggage make a difference? | What's the hard way?
a : With a full pail you want more distance and fewer stairs. | Explaining why long is quicker with a sore knee.


scene chalk_cost
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put the price of wrapping where folks can see it. | A cheap jug's dear if it arrives in seven pieces.
b : Even for one bowl? | The pieces do have their uses.
a : Especially for one. No need to make a small purchase mysterious. | I make maps from them. Nobody ought to pay jug prices for a map.


scene times_low
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : There's less going round. You feel it in what gets mended. | I'd sooner teach a repair in a lean spell.
b : More patched handles? | Than sell a replacement?
a : Worn ones, kept on till there's barely a finger's grip. | Yes. You'll remember who kept the old one working.


scene wagons_out
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late|raided
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : A late wagon leaves a hole no amount of careful stacking will hide. | Roads are giving us grief again, it seems.
b : Expecting something yourself? | Any word how far out?
a : I'd like wrapping straw. There are plenty of wolves with worse needs. | No. I'd mark the spot if anybody had seen it.


scene stand_talk
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't draw a street till I've stood in it. Gossip gets the same treatment. | There's a rumour taking shape on this tray.
b : So you'll say nothing? | Why is there a chip missing?
a : I could talk a day about what I actually know. Try me. | That's the bit that's meant to be true. Haven't found it yet.


scene festival_mat
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Before a dance I inspect the paving. | I'd mark a dance with chips just to see the pattern.
b : You afraid of a tumble? | What about the dancers?
a : Afraid? No. Particular about which direction I tumble in. | They'd step all over it. That's why I'd draw it afterwards.


scene early_break
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Early light shows every raised lip in a path. | Dawn gives my little map enormous shadows.
b : Shadows do the work for you. | How big are the hills?
a : Some of it. I still have to get down and look. | Tall enough to make a breakfast crumb look like the keep.


scene old_injury
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw sitting upright and look at it from below when I'm done. | Stiff knees teach a wolf more about stairs than a ruler can.
b : Why go down twice? | Has the ruler got it wrong?
a : A good idea from above can be a nuisance at paw level. | No. It just never had to climb the stairs it measured.


scene card_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with the box of little pieces. | I like a route best when I can show it to #self.friend#.
b : Even the bits you haven't placed? | Is it a present, then?
a : Particularly those. Takes some trust to show an untidy mind. | The walk is. I keep the chips for making the next one.


scene dry_relief
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A dry sill is enough to make me thank the Bright One. | I believe a prayer can be practical.
b : A little thing to give thanks for. | Practical how?
a : Lovely, isn't it? Don't have to wait for a miracle. | Dry somebody off first. Then there's breath for talking.


scene dream_pour
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dreamt the town tilted and everything on my map stayed put. | In my dream the streets flowed and the water stood still.
b : Which did you fix? | How did you cross?
a : The map. Couldn't very well lift a town before breakfast. | Hopped from puddle to puddle. Best walk I've ever slept through.


scene last_piece
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've one piece with no street to go with it. | A chip the colour of cream belongs somewhere on this plan.
b : Will you look for a new street? | Could it be a square?
a : Yes. It's a good excuse for taking a walk. | A very small one. Room for you, me and a considerable argument.


story bowlroute [topic=memories|land self.age>=25]
  : I once laid out a route to a wedding on a tray. Took nearly all the breakfast things to get the houses right.
  : When the guest had gone, I drank my tea round three saucers and a little hill of spoons.
  b : Did the guest find the wedding?
  : Back just after dinner, with a slice of cake. A map with a sweet return journey.


story friedplan [topic=food|memories]
  : I tried making a little plan of a lane in sticky cake crumbs once.
  : The slope looked splendid. Then the whole lane slid slowly towards the edge of the plate.
  b : What did you do about the landslip?
  : Ate uphill. Had the street quite stable when I finally reached the square.


story quarrel_heel [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I borrowed a boot to represent a great hall on my map. Good tall heel and the right shape of toe.
  : Its owner hopped up and asked what time the council rose.
  b : Did you let the council finish?
  : Sent them home early. A hop on wet paving's too high a price for civic business.


story lime_line [topic=work|memories self.job=merchant self.age>=25]
  : My first case had a fine white line all round the lid. Very pleased with how tidy it looked.
  : Every mile rubbed off a little white. By the end the lid looked like a grin with two teeth.
  b : A lesson in wrapping?
  : And in judging the box after the journey. Everything looks well packed before the first jolt.


story wrong_slope [topic=smalltalk|memories]
  : I turned my tray round to show a walker the last turn, then forgot I'd turned it.
  : Both of us stood pointing in opposite directions and both of us were right about the tray.
  b : Who gave way first?
  : Set it on the actual step. The loose pieces voted downhill. We agreed to be guided by the majority.


rule @cratecry
when concept=bark self.job=merchant working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Handle inside the wrap, please! It likes to travel attached. | Spare straw goes low. The top can look after itself.


rule @rainrim
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Brown water's on the move. Pick the high edge! | Careful at the seam. That's deeper than a shine.


rule @chipcry
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There goes half my hill under that heel! | This blue chip has a whole street's work to do.


rule @snowshard
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say White on white! I'll need the blue pieces today. | Leave that patch smooth till I see where it sags.


rule @matcry
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe your pads twice if one pass leaves a print! | Dry side of the mat, if you please.


rule @honeycry
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sticky crumbs! Best sort of packing problem. | Anyone claiming the bit with the golden edge?

dlg resident.hub : Tell me where you'd like to end up. I can usually find a way there.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you'll recognise the blue chip. I've moved the rest.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Don't step on my work while we're deciding whether to be civil.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Keep the pale bits in view as you approach. Saves a lot of crunching.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I help at #self.workplace#. I have opinions on every parcel that leaves.
dlg resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I've other accomplishments if you've the spare hour.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I've one piece I can place. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Empty tray, as far as other wolves' business goes.
dlg resident.bye : Off you go. High way there, easy way home.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize# takes a steady paw. Set your questions down one at a time.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=no] : The learning place is occupied. There's still room to ask about the work.
dlg master.work : Keeping the sound pieces sound is most of the trick. Noise tells you when you've packed the pieces too close.
dlg master.wages : Learning pays in what your paws can do. What you make yourself is yours to sell.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : One learning place, filled by somebody I trust. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.refused : I can only give you the actual reason. #topic.why#.
dlg master.bye : Bring your sharp questions back another day. Blunt ones too.
graft resident.hub
choice Could you show me a street in those pieces? -> chipstreet
node chipstreet
say Here's the turn and here's the gutter. Put a claw at the top and travel down. Feel that snag? That's somebody's bad afternoon.
mood keen
free
choice What if I move the gutter? -> chipgutter
choice I'll remember the snag. -> hub
node chipgutter
say You've given the house beside it a cellar full of water. Architects seldom get such a prompt review.
choice Let's put it back. -> hub
choice I'd better go now. -> bye
graft master.learn
choice How can I tell if a case is packed well? -> testcase
node testcase
say Try to shift one parcel with a claw. It ought to give just slightly, then settle back into the space made for it.
choice What if the whole row moves? -> testrow
choice I'll try that. -> learn
node testrow
say Take it out and lay another twist of straw down the side. Nobody thanks you for delivering a case of expensive little maps.
choice Back to the trade. -> learn
choice That's enough for me. -> bye
